  "content": "## Finding files and joining Workspace products\n\nDrive searches file data; operation discovery searches API capabilities.\nUse file ids from reads or Drive URLs. The same id identifies a Google Doc,\nSheet, Slides deck or Form in its product connector. Shared-drive ids identify\nmembership and the root folder; folder parents determine inherited access.\nA missing file and a file the delegated user cannot see fail alike.\n\nDrive query values use single quotes: `name contains 'budget'`,\n`mimeType = 'application/pdf'`, `'folder_123' in parents`, or\n`modifiedTime > '2026-01-01T00:00:00'`. Trashed files are excluded by default.\n`incompleteSearch: true` means Google did not search every corpus; narrow the\nquery or choose a single shared drive. It is never an exact count.\n\n## Content and file decisions\n\nThe content workflow exports Docs as Markdown, Sheets as CSV of the first\nsheet only, and Slides as text. Other text files retain their declared charset.\nSmall binary files can be returned as base64. A drawing, unsupported native\nfile, folder, shortcut or oversized binary returns an unavailable explanation.\nFor a shortcut, read its target id instead. Drive exports at most 10 MB.\n\nContent containing sent credentials is withheld as a whole binary value; there\nis no partial-content recovery around that boundary. Withheld MIME, shortcut,\nfolder or parent metadata cannot decide a subsequent read or move. Re-read\nthrough a safe source before trying the workflow again.\n\n## Access and recovery\n\nA file or copy inherits its destination folder's access. Read permission holders\nbefore moving, copying or creating in a shared folder, and read them again after\nchanging access. Inherited permissions name the parent folder or shared drive\nthat must be changed instead. An owner cannot be removed or replaced here.\n\nAll new grants use `share_file`, which sends no notification email by default.\nConfirm intent before granting `anyone` or domain access. Permission creation\nthrough the hatch is refused, including public-link grants; the named workflow\nowns grantee validation and notification behavior.\n\nContent updates replace the complete content. A create with an uncertain outcome\nneeds a search for the intended file before another create. Recoverable trash\ncan be restored for 30 days. Permanent deletion, ownership transfer, watch\nregistration, credential minting and generic media transport are outside the\nhatch. Use the named content and upload workflows for bounded bytes.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** a paged `list_*` or `search_*` read takes `limit` (default 25, at most 100) and `cursor`. While `page.hasMore` is true, pass `page.nextCursor` back unchanged as `cursor`; the last page has no `nextCursor`.\n- **Paging:** on a paged hatch read, keep the original method, path, filters, limit and fields. Pass `page.nextCursor` unchanged as the top-level `cursor`; omit raw anchors on continuations. The last page has `page.hasMore: false` and no `nextCursor`. If `page.hasMore` is true without a cursor, the data is incomplete and continuation could not be confined.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Hatch:** `drive_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `drive_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `drive_api_read` calls a reviewed read. `drive_api_write` calls a reviewed write; the host may ask the user to confirm it. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused; these are refused by design: `DELETE /drives/{driveId}`, `DELETE /files/trash`, `DELETE /files/{fileId}/comments/{commentId}/replies/{replyId}`, `DELETE /files/{fileId}/comments/{commentId}`, `DELETE /files/{fileId}/revisions/{revisionId}`, `DELETE /files/{fileId}`, `DELETE /teamdrives/{teamDriveId}`, `GET /apps/{appId}`, `GET /apps`, `GET /changes/startPageToken`, `GET /changes`, `GET /drives/{driveId}`, `GET /files/generateCseToken`, `GET /files/generateIds`, `GET /files/{fileId}/accessproposals/{proposalId}`, `GET /files/{fileId}/accessproposals`, `GET /files/{fileId}/approvals/{approvalId}`, `GET /files/{fileId}/approvals`, `GET /files/{fileId}/comments/{commentId}/replies/{replyId}`, `GET /files/{fileId}/comments/{commentId}/replies`, `GET /files/{fileId}/comments/{commentId}`, `GET /files/{fileId}/comments`, `GET /files/{fileId}/export`, `GET /files/{fileId}/listLabels`, `GET /operations/{name}`, `GET /teamdrives/{teamDriveId}`, `GET /teamdrives`, `PATCH /drives/{driveId}`, `PATCH /files/{fileId}/comments/{commentId}/replies/{replyId}`, `PATCH /files/{fileId}/comments/{commentId}`, `PATCH /files/{fileId}/revisions/{revisionId}`, `PATCH /teamdrives/{teamDriveId}`, `POST /changes/watch`, `POST /channels/stop`, `POST /drives/{driveId}/hide`, `POST /drives/{driveId}/unhide`, `POST /drives`, `POST /files/{fileId}/accessproposals/{proposalId}:resolve`, `POST /files/{fileId}/approvals/{approvalId}:approve`, `POST /files/{fileId}/approvals/{approvalId}:cancel`, `POST /files/{fileId}/approvals/{approvalId}:comment`, `POST /files/{fileId}/approvals/{approvalId}:decline`, `POST /files/{fileId}/approvals/{approvalId}:reassign`, `POST /files/{fileId}/approvals:start`, `POST /files/{fileId}/comments/{commentId}/replies`, `POST /files/{fileId}/comments`, `POST /files/{fileId}/download`, `POST /files/{fileId}/modifyLabels`, `POST /files/{fileId}/permissions`, `POST /files/{fileId}/watch`, `POST /teamdrives`.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. Writes take no idempotency key.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. An unknown id, or one these credentials cannot reach, fails as `connector_call_failed`; this API does not tell the two apart. `conflict` means: A Drive source page changed before its local cursor resumed..\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.",
